---
source: crates/git-aggregate-rs/tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(output.stdout).unwrap()"
---
Aggregate git branches and pull requests from repos.yaml (gitaggregate drop-in)

Usage: git-aggregate-rs [OPTIONS] [ACTION]

Arguments:
  [ACTION]
          Action to run

          Possible values:
          - aggregate:       Fetch and merge the configured branches and pull requests
          - show-closed-prs: List pull requests in the configuration that are closed or merged
          - show-all-prs:    List every pull request in the configuration with its state
          
          [default: aggregate]

Options:
  -c, --config <FILE>
          Path to the repositories file
          
          [default: repos.yaml]

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Number of repositories to process in parallel
          
          [default: 1]

  -d, --dirmatch <GLOB>
          Only process target directories matching this glob

  -p, --push
          Push each aggregated target branch to its remote

      --expand-env
          Expand `$VAR` and `${VAR}` in the repositories file

  -e, --env-file <FILE>
          Load environment variables from FILE before expanding

  -f, --force
          Discard local changes in the target directories

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Logging verbosity

          Possible values:
          - debug:   Everything, including fetch and merge details
          - info:    Progress per repository
          - warning: Warnings and errors
          - error:   Errors only
          
          [default: info]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also honors `NO_COLOR`)

      --allow-shell
          Allow `shell_command_after` entries to run (off by default)

      --lock <FILE>
          Write a reproducible lockfile with the resolved commits

      --mergiraf
          Use mergiraf for syntax-aware conflict resolution

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
